# RTTM generated by tests/eval/docx_to_rttm.py from a hand-typed .docx
# transcript, not this app's own export - see that script's module
# docstring for the full method.
# Source docx: mp3_test/diarization_test/test#2/אבי ונאור תמלול.docx
# Source audio: mp3_test/diarization_test/test#2/הקלטת שיחה אבי מורלי זוק_240829_150856.m4a
# Colour-coding origin: the docx's own text-colour convention (verified by
# hand, not assumed) - a "הדוברים: אבי נאור" header row colours אבי's name
# purple (RGB A02B93) and leaves נאור in the run's default colour (no
# w:color at all). Every speech paragraph after it follows the same
# convention, run by run.
# Alignment method: the matching audio was transcribed with this app's own
# Transcriber (ivrit-turbo, Hebrew) for precise word timings, then each of
# the docx's ~24s block markers ("M:SS - M:SS", bidi-isolated) was used as a
# HARD window (+/-3s pad) inside which that block's coloured lines were
# matched onto the transcribed words via difflib.SequenceMatcher over
# tests/eval/hebrew_metrics's normalised tokens. Matched turns were merged
# with tests/eval/transcript_to_rttm.py's own merge_turns (0.5s max gap,
# DIARIZATION_MIN_DURATION_OFF) - the same merge rule as every other RTTM
# fixture in this directory.
#
# Validation (Deliverable 2, see tests/test_docx_to_rttm.py + the module
# docstring of tests/eval/docx_to_rttm.py for the method): test#1's known-good
# tests/eval/fixtures/diarization/hebrew_2spk.rttm was bucketed into
# synthetic ~24s blocks with its true per-utterance timings DISCARDED (same
# shape as a real docx: text + a coarse block window, nothing finer), then
# reconstructed by this same aligner and scored against the true RTTM:
#   coverage: 95/100 synthetic lines matched
#   DER=0.2846 (missed=112.06s, false_alarm=13.70s, confusion=2.96s,
#               total_ref=452.36s)
#   per-speaker time agreement (speaker_recall): יאיר_שיזף=0.66, נאור_בוסי=0.95
# Confusion - the ONE component Deliverable 4's embedding-model comparison
# actually depends on - reconstructs almost exactly right: 2.96s wrong out of
# 452.36s is 99.3% correct speaker attribution. The error that IS large,
# missed_speech, is a systematic UNDERCOUNT of true speech duration (a
# matched line's span is bounded by the words that text-matched inside it,
# not by where the speaker's turn actually started/ended - a trailing filler
# word the model transcribed slightly differently is common and shrinks the
# span), not a misattribution between the two speakers. An intra-block
# gap-fill heuristic was tried to close this gap and made DER WORSE (0.3442,
# false_alarm more than tripled) - see DEFAULT_MAX_INTRA_BLOCK_FILL_GAP in
# docx_to_rttm.py - so it ships disabled. Net conclusion: absolute DER on
# this fixture is not directly comparable to a hand-drawn reference (the
# same caveat tests/eval/transcript_to_rttm.py's header already carries for
# hebrew_2spk.rttm, for an unrelated reason - segment boundaries there, text-
# matched spans here), but A/B comparisons BETWEEN diarization
# configurations - confusion, per-speaker recall - stay meaningful, which is
# exactly what Deliverable 4 measures.
#
# This fixture's own coverage: 53/56 docx lines matched (94.6%), 3 dropped
# for falling below --min-line-coverage=0.5 (text present in the docx that
# the aligner could not confidently place in time, and therefore left out
# rather than guessed).
